{"seq":33,"at":"2026-10-23","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0751"},"reason":"Body extended in all three languages (new passage and table row) to carry the new fact f28002 (caliph); a few connecting phrases adjusted so the page still reads as one.","by":"fact-count-rework","sources":[{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caliphate"}],"changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",959],["+","\n\nThe oldest of these political words is caliph, from the Arabic khalīfa, “successor” or “deputy”. After Muhammad's death in 632 the leaders of the Muslim community styled themselves successors of the Messenger of God, and the title passed through the Umayyad and Abbasid dynasties to the Ottoman sultans, until the Turkish Republic abolished the caliphate on 3 March 1924. When the so-called Islamic State proclaimed a new caliphate in 2014, it was deliberately reviving a title that had stood vacant for ninety years."]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",891],["+","\n\nDas älteste dieser politischen Wörter ist Kalif, vom arabischen chalīfa, „Nachfolger“ oder „Stellvertreter“. Nach Mohammeds Tod im Jahr 632 nannten sich die Führer der muslimischen Gemeinschaft Nachfolger des Gesandten Gottes, und der Titel ging über die Dynastien der Umayyaden und Abbasiden auf die osmanischen Sultane über, bis die Türkische Republik das Kalifat am 3. März 1924 abschaffte. Als der sogenannte Islamische Staat 2014 ein neues Kalifat ausrief, belebte er bewusst einen Titel wieder, der neunzig Jahre lang unbesetzt gewesen war."]]},{"field":"bodyRu","diff":[["=",829],["+","\n\nСамое старое из этих политических слов — халиф, от арабского «халифа», то есть «преемник» или «заместитель». После смерти Мухаммеда в 632 году предводители мусульманской общины называли себя преемниками Посланника Бога, и титул перешёл через династии Омейядов и Аббасидов к османским султанам, пока Турецкая Республика не упразднила халифат 3 марта 1924 года. Когда так называемое «Исламское государство» в 2014 году провозгласило новый халифат, оно сознательно возрождало титул, пустовавший девяносто лет."]]}],"hash":"7c06b6a2d2b4"},
{"seq":34,"at":"2026-10-23","kind":"created","target":{"type":"fact","id":"f28002"},"reason":"New researched question integrated into the article body: “Caliph” is the oldest and most consequential Arabic political word, revived in the news by the Islamic State, and was missing.","by":"fact-count-rework","sources":[{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caliphate"}],"changes":[{"field":"answerEn","new":"caliph"},{"field":"answerDe","new":"Kalif"},{"field":"answerRu","new":"халиф"},{"field":"spans","new":{"en":[2930,6],"de":[3284,5],"ru":[2938,5]}},{"field":"timeline","new":{"kind":"event","start":"1924-03-03","end":null,"precision":"day","approx":false,"ongoing":false,"labelEn":"The Turkish Republic abolishes the caliphate","labelDe":"Die Türkische Republik schafft das Kalifat ab","labelRu":"Турецкая Республика упраздняет халифат"}},{"field":"source","new":{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caliphate","title":"Caliphate – Wikipedia","lang":"en"}}],"hash":"a9acca1eeb75"},
{"seq":35,"at":"2026-10-23","kind":"created","target":{"type":"wording","id":"w27002"},"reason":"Open question for the new fact f28002 (answer: caliph).","by":"fact-count-rework","changes":[{"field":"en","new":"Which title, from the Arabic word for “successor”, did the leaders of the Muslim community bear from Muhammad's death until Turkey abolished the office in 1924?"},{"field":"de","new":"Welchen Titel, abgeleitet vom arabischen Wort für „Nachfolger“, trugen die Führer der muslimischen Gemeinschaft von Mohammeds Tod bis zur Abschaffung des Amtes durch die Türkei 1924?"},{"field":"ru","new":"Какой титул, происходящий от арабского слова «преемник», носили предводители мусульманской общины со смерти Мухаммеда до упразднения этой должности Турцией в 1924 году?"},{"field":"origin","new":"generated"},{"field":"fact","new":"f28002"}],"hash":"e7508336392d"},
